CHANGELOG = '## [0.257.0] - a building\'s package carries its drawings\n\n**The factory\'s roadmap 296.** The walker, of roadmap 293\'s exploded axonometric, asked where it is seen: "both" -- a\nreview page and a level\'s export -- "It could even get into the game where the players can \'scope out\' the level and\nsee the buildings the level assembles". A building\'s files reach a level only through\n`portable_building.build_package` (Level Factory\'s presentation compose, then its export\'s copy into `lot/<id>/`), and\nno drawing went that way: the plans and the axonometric were written only into the ignored `build/floorplans/`, by\n`validate.py`.\n\n### Added\n- **`build_package(..., spec_path=)`**: named the spec the building was built from, the package draws it into\n  `drawings/` (`package_drawings`) -- the exploded axonometric and a plan a storey (`floor<n>`, a basement\n  `floorB<depth>`), each beside a `.import` that keeps it as the file it is (`KEEP_IMPORT`), and `drawings.json`\n  naming them -- and records it in its manifest under `drawings`. Drawn from the spec when the package is composed, so\n  a package never carries a drawing older than its building. Named no spec, a package is what it was. `--spec` on the\n  command line.\n- **A facade gets the record and the reason, no drawing**: a street wall with no interior, never entered, whose\n  axonometric is an empty walled box (gs_facade_rowhome and gs_midrise_a drawn and read, 2026-10-21).\n- **How a drawing ships, measured on Godot 4.7, headless** (the factory\'s `patches/dc_drawings/keep_probe.py`): left\n  to the default import, deli_a03\'s axonometric becomes a 136,248-byte texture in every level that carries it, for a\n  screen no game has built yet; with the keep `.import` beside it none is made, the `.import` comes back as written,\n  and a game still reads the file with `FileAccess` and draws it with `Image.load_svg_from_string` (674 x 1197, no\n  error), at the size its own screen wants.\n\n### Fixed\n- **An axonometric\'s canvas holds its own text.** The canvas was the drawing\'s extent alone, and on a small building\n  -- a facade, 275 px -- the title, the two lines under it and the legend ran off its right edge: the facade\'s last\n  legend word began at 466 px. The widest of them now sets a floor under the width, each measured as it is written\n  (`CHAR_EM`, `CHAR_EM_BOLD`; the legend, `LEGEND`, by its own steps); a drawing wide enough before is drawn as\n  before.\n\n### Tests\n- **test_package_drawings.py**, new, four: the keep `.import` is the one Godot left as written; deli_a03\'s package\n  carries its axonometric and three plans, each its renderer\'s drawing of the spec, each beside a keep `.import`,\n  named in `drawings.json`; a facade\'s carries the reason and no drawing; `build_package` draws when named a spec and\n  draws nothing when not. On 0.256.0 all four fail on the missing names.\n- **test_axonometric.py**, one more: every line of text fits its canvas, on a facade, a midrise, office and deli_a03\n  -- the legend first, by its own steps, so on 0.256.0 it fails on behaviour (the facade\'s legend ends past its 275\n  px) and not on a name (the factory\'s `patches/dc_drawings/prove_tests_on_0256.out.txt`).\n\n### Measured, kept\n- **Left** (the factory\'s roadmap 296): Level Factory naming the spec of each building it composes, and an index of a\n  level\'s buildings at its package\'s root; a review page built from a cold run\'s package; the in-game screen, which is\n  the game\'s.\n- **Seen while reading**: `floorplan.write_floorplans` names every basement `floorB`, so a building with two would\n  write one plan over the other; none in the library has two (read 2026-10-21), and a package names its plans by\n  depth.\n\n'
OLD_VERSION, NEW_VERSION = 'Deli Counter 0.256.0', 'Deli Counter 0.257.0'


def _sha(b):
    return hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()[:16]


def _read(name):
    """The file's LF text and whether it is CRLF on disk; refuses mixed endings and a file that is not the pinned one."""
    raw = (REPO / name).read_bytes()
    crlf, lf = raw.count(b"\r\n"), raw.count(b"\n")
    if crlf not in (0, lf):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s has mixed line endings (%d CRLF of %d); nothing written"
                         % (name, crlf, lf))
    text = raw.decode("utf-8").replace("\r\n", "\n")
    if _sha(text.encode("utf-8")) != PINS[name]:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s is %s, not the %s this patch was written against; nothing "
                         "written" % (name, _sha(text.encode("utf-8")), PINS[name]))
    return text, crlf > 0


def main(argv):
    # every file worked out and checked before any is written
    out = {}
    for name, edits in EDITS.items():
        text, crlf = _read(name)
        for what, old, new in edits:
            if text.count(old) != 1:
                raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s: the anchor at %s is there %d times; nothing written"
                                 % (name, what, text.count(old)))
            text = text.replace(old, new)
        out[name] = text.replace("\n", "\r\n") if crlf else text
    # a refurnished spec is carried whole, the file it replaces pinned like any other
    for name, text in REPLACED.items():
        _old, crlf = _read(name)
        out[name] = text.replace("\n", "\r\n") if crlf else text
    for name in NEW_FILES:
        if (REPO / name).exists():
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s exists already; nothing written" % name)
    v = REPO / "VERSION"
    if v.read_bytes().decode("utf-8") != OLD_VERSION:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: VERSION reads %r, not %s; nothing written" % (v.read_text(), OLD_VERSION))
    cl = REPO / "CHANGELOG.md"
    craw = cl.read_bytes()
    if b"\r\n" in craw or not craw.startswith(b"## [" + OLD_VERSION.split()[-1].encode() + b"]"):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: CHANGELOG.md is not LF opening on %s; nothing written" % OLD_VERSION)
    for name, text in out.items():
        (REPO / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    for name, text in NEW_FILES.items():
        (REPO / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    v.write_bytes(NEW_VERSION.encode("utf-8"))
    cl.write_bytes(CHANGELOG.encode("utf-8") + craw)
    print("%s applied: %d files edited, %d written, VERSION, CHANGELOG. Now, in deli_counter/: build.py --all, "
          "suite" % (NEW_VERSION, len(out), len(NEW_FILES)))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
